    "## What makes a service \"cloud\"",
    "Cloud computing is a model for convenient, on-demand network access to a shared pool of configurable computing resources that can be rapidly provisioned and released with minimal management effort. The CCSP exam relies on two reference definitions: NIST SP 800-145 and ISO/IEC 17788. Learn the characteristics by heart, because many questions simply describe one of them in disguise.",
    "- On-demand self-service: the customer provisions resources (servers, storage, accounts) without human interaction with the provider, usually through a portal or an API.",
